{"type":"emit_inbound","label":"notification:session/update:user_message_chunk","frame":{"kind":"notification","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"sess_00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","update":{"content":{"text":"<t3_code_instructions>\n## T3 Code interaction mode: Default\n\nPrefer making reasonable assumptions and carrying out the user's request. Ask a concise question only when a missing user decision would materially change the result. Treat this mode as active until T3 Code supplies a different interaction-mode instruction.\n</t3_code_instructions>\n\n<user_request>\nUse the terminal tool for each step and write no text until step 4.\n1. Run `seq 1 1500` in the foreground.\n2. Run `seq 1501 3000` in the foreground.\n3. Start `sleep 5 && echo compact-probe-done` as a background process with notify set to true. Do not wait for it.\n4. Reply with exactly: compact probe first turn\nWhen that background process's completion notification arrives, reply with exactly: A_REPORTED\n</user_request>\n<runtime_info>In case you're asked: you are running in T3 Code through the Hermes harness, as custom:cliproxyapi-claude:claude-haiku-5-5. No need to mention this otherwise. You can embed images, video, and audio in your response using Markdown image syntax with absolute file paths. Link any other file you produce using its absolute path so the user can open it in T3 Code's files viewer.</runtime_info>\n\n<pull_request_linking>\nLink each PR you create, take over, or push to: link_pull_request, or link_pull_requests for several, full URL, every stack layer, as your next call. Host tools do not link for you. If linking fails, say so. Skip PRs you only read or review, and PRs named only as background. Call watch_pull_request when asked to monitor or babysit, or when work you were asked to do, such as a merge, still waits on checks or reviews, even after an earlier unwatch. Finish any needed branch update and push first, then watch and end your turn. Otherwise act now or hand back. Delegated children never watch, even if the brief says babysit. After PR work, a child's last line is: PR <full URL>, head <SHA>, checks and reviews <state>. Links and watches persist across pushes. For PR waits, no sleep, loops, gh --watch, Monitor or ScheduleWakeup. Before handback, call unwatch_pull_request on any PR you watch.\n</pull_request_linking>","type":"text"},"sessionUpdate":"user_message_chunk"}}}}
